  "body": "`OffscreenCanvas` takes type annotated parameters in its constructor.\r\n```\r\nConstructor([EnforceRange] unsigned long long width, [EnforceRange] unsigned long long height)\r\n```\r\nbeside it, the corresponding attributes do not have the type annotation.\r\n```\r\nattribute unsigned long long width;\r\nattribute unsigned long long height;\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis mismatching allows to set invalid values on them (and fallback to valid values with modulus operation)\r\n```\r\nvar a = new OffscreenCanvas(-1, -1);  // throws error, because of [EnforceRange]\r\nvar b = new OffscreenCanvas(0, 0);\r\nb.width = -1;  // it accepts without errors.\r\n```\r\nIt is confusing, and WPT test expects to thow errors on setting invalid values on these attibutes.\r\n\r\nHence the types of `width` and `height` should be annotated with `[EnforceRange]`.",
